# 🗄️ Database Management System

## Database Name

```sql
mediconnect_db
```

The database is designed using a relational database model.

The database stores information related to users, donors, blood groups, blood requests, blood banks, inventory, donations, notifications, and verification records.

The proposed database design uses primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, check constraints, indexes, and transactions to maintain data consistency and integrity.

---

## 📊 Proposed Database Tables

### 1. Users

Stores common information about all registered users.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| user_id | Primary Key |
| full_name | User's full name |
| email | Unique email address |
| phone | Contact number |
| password_hash | Hashed password |
| role_id | Foreign Key |
| created_at | Registration date |
| account_status | Account status |

### 2. Roles

Stores different roles available in the system.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| role_id | Primary Key |
| role_name | Patient, Donor, Hospital, Blood Bank, Admin |

### 3. Donors

Stores donor-specific information.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| donor_id | Primary Key |
| user_id | Foreign Key |
| blood_group_id | Foreign Key |
| city | Donor's city |
| state | Donor's state |
| address | Donor's address |
| availability_status | Availability |
| last_donation_date | Previous donation date |
| verification_status | Verification status |

### 4. Blood_Groups

Stores available blood group classifications.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| blood_group_id | Primary Key |
| blood_group_name | A+, A-, B+, B-, AB+, AB-, O+, O- |

### 5. Blood_Requests

Stores emergency blood requests.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| request_id | Primary Key |
| requester_id | Foreign Key |
| hospital_id | Foreign Key |
| blood_group_id | Foreign Key |
| component_type | Required blood component |
| quantity | Required quantity |
| city | Required location |
| urgency_level | Normal, Urgent, Critical |
| required_date | Required date |
| request_status | Current status |
| created_at | Request creation time |

### 6. Donor_Matches

Stores potential donor matches for blood requests.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| match_id | Primary Key |
| request_id | Foreign Key |
| donor_id | Foreign Key |
| match_status | Pending, Accepted, Declined |
| matched_at | Match creation time |
| response_time | Donor response time |

### 7. Blood_Banks

Stores registered blood bank information.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| blood_bank_id | Primary Key |
| name | Blood bank name |
| registration_number | Registration number |
| address | Blood bank address |
| city | City |
| phone | Contact number |
| verification_status | Verification status |

### 8. Blood_Inventory

Stores blood bank stock information.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| inventory_id | Primary Key |
| blood_bank_id | Foreign Key |
| blood_group_id | Foreign Key |
| component_type | Blood component |
| quantity | Available quantity |
| expiry_date | Expiry date |
| last_updated | Last stock update |

### 9. Donations

Stores donation history records.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| donation_id | Primary Key |
| donor_id | Foreign Key |
| blood_bank_id | Foreign Key |
| donation_date | Donation date |
| component_type | Donated component |
| quantity | Quantity donated |
| donation_status | Donation status |

### 10. Hospitals

Stores registered hospital details.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| hospital_id | Primary Key |
| hospital_name | Hospital name |
| registration_number | Registration number |
| address | Hospital address |
| city | City |
| contact_number | Contact number |
| verification_status | Verification status |

### 11. Notifications

Stores notification records.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| notification_id | Primary Key |
| user_id | Foreign Key |
| request_id | Foreign Key |
| message | Notification message |
| notification_type | Notification category |
| is_read | Read status |
| created_at | Notification time |

### 12. Verification_Records

Stores verification details of users and organizations.

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| verification_id | Primary Key |
| user_id | Foreign Key |
| entity_type | Donor, Hospital, Blood Bank |
| verification_status | Pending, Verified, Rejected |
| verified_by | Admin ID |
| verified_at | Verification date |

---

## 🔗 Database Relationships

The proposed database follows relational database principles.

### Relationship Structure

- One Role can be assigned to multiple Users.
- One User can have one Donor Profile.
- One Blood Group can be associated with multiple Donors.
- One User can create multiple Blood Requests.
- One Blood Request can have multiple Donor Matches.
- One Donor can be associated with multiple Donor Matches.
- One Blood Bank can maintain multiple Inventory Records.
- One Blood Group can have multiple Inventory Records.
- One Donor can have multiple Donation Records.
- One Hospital can create multiple Blood Requests.
- One User can receive multiple Notifications.

### Relationship Types

| Relationship | Type |
|---|---|
| Roles → Users | One-to-Many |
| Users → Donors | One-to-One |
| Blood Groups → Donors | One-to-Many |
| Users → Blood Requests | One-to-Many |
| Blood Requests → Donor Matches | One-to-Many |
| Donors → Donor Matches | One-to-Many |
| Blood Banks → Inventory | One-to-Many |
| Blood Groups → Inventory | One-to-Many |
| Donors → Donations | One-to-Many |
| Hospitals → Blood Requests | One-to-Many |

---

