# ⚙️ Installation and Setup

> The following setup instructions represent the planned development environment. Commands and configuration may change as the application is developed.

## Prerequisites

Install the following software:

- Node.js
- npm
- MySQL Server
- MySQL Workbench
- Visual Studio Code
- Git

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/MediConnect.git
```

```bash
cd MediConnect
```

## 2. Frontend Setup

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

The frontend will run locally using Vite.

## 3. Backend Setup

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file:

```env
PORT=5000

DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_mysql_password
DB_NAME=mediconnect_db

JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
```

Start the backend:

```bash
npm run dev
```

## 4. Database Setup

Open MySQL Workbench.

Create the database:

```sql
CREATE DATABASE mediconnect_db;
```

Select the database:

```sql
USE mediconnect_db;
```

Execute the SQL files in the database folder after they are created.

